course: dictionary
lesson: 2198
title: Councillors and councils
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A council is a group of people who make decisions for an area, such as a town or city. «The council is the local government that looks after roads, parks, bins, libraries and planning.» Local government means the people who run services close to where you live.
explain: The people who sit on a council are called councillors. «Councillors are elected by local people.» Elected means people in the area vote for them, and then the councillors make decisions for everyone there.
explain: Context helps again. «Council meetings are usually open to the public» tells you that ordinary people can come and watch. A word like «school councillor» uses the same idea on a smaller scale: a pupil who sits on a school council.
fact: A councillor is a member of a council.
fact: «Councillor» means a person elected to sit on a council and make decisions for an area.
fact: «Council» means a local group that runs services such as bins, parks, libraries and roads.
fact: Pupils may be elected as class or school councillors.
fact: You can write to your councillor about a problem, such as a broken streetlight.
exercise: «Councillors are elected by local people.» What does elected mean here? | Given money for free | Chosen by a teacher alone | *Chosen by people voting | Left out of the group
exercise: Maya has a broken streetlight on her road. Who could she write to? | The lollipop lady | *Her local councillor | Her swimming coach | The head teacher at her school
exercise: «Council meetings are usually open to the public.» What does open to the public mean? | *Anyone can come and watch | Only councillors can come | Only for children | Closed on Sundays
test: Which of these does a council look after? | The planets | The weather | *Bins
test: What is a school councillor? | *A pupil elected to sit on a school council | A dinner lady | A teacher who marks homework
exam: What do councillors do for an area? | Sleep in the town hall | Cook lunch in schools | *Make decisions for it, such as about roads and parks | Only sell tickets for the bus
